# modules-v2-graph U3 (D14): Buffer is no longer a bare-name registration, so
# compiled WITHOUT the prelude, `Buffer b = ...` fails at the DECLARATION during
# type resolution (findType returns null). U6b-2 sharpened the message: it now
# names the unresolved type at the type token ("unknown type 'Buffer' ...")
# instead of the generic "Failed parse varible" at the operator column.
^[^:]+\.b:[0-9]+:[0-9]+: error: unknown type 'Buffer' in variable declaration$
